          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"flaubert-madame-bovary-d0ec3752ec68\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.92,\"analysis\":\"The direct reply “Je t’aime!” straightforwardly avows that the speaker loves the addressee. Neither the words nor the supplied context independently establish a commitment or relational undertaking. The exclamation mark and accompanying embrace indicate affective intensity but do not show that the words are a reflex-like expressive discharge rather than an emphatic avowal.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The very short extract does not establish the avowal’s sincerity or broader interpersonal purpose, but those uncertainties do not alter its strongly truth-conditional force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"A female character directly says “Je t’aime!” to the person around whose neck she then puts her arms; the narrator presents it as her spoken reply.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The speech tag “répondit-elle” frames the utterance as an answer, while her embrace reinforces its affectionate and emotionally emphatic delivery. The extract provides no independent evidence of promising, undertaking an obligation, or involuntarily blurting out the words. Any possible sincerity, manipulation, or narrative irony remains unresolved by the supplied context.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"local-1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Je t’aime!”\",\"supports\":\"The conventional propositional content directly presents the speaker’s love for the addressee as true, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"local-2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“répondit-elle”\",\"supports\":\"The narrator identifies the utterance as her direct spoken reply, supporting direct status and an avowal-like reading.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"local-3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“en lui passant les bras autour du cou”\",\"supports\":\"The accompanying embrace supports affectionate intensity but supplies no independent evidence for performative undertaking or reflex-like expressive force.\",\"confidence\":0.9}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core utterance as an avowal of love. The embrace and exclamatory punctuation can remain contextual features of delivery without requiring P, E, or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
